[Music]  the royal family is often described as  the firm and much like any company there  are many people involved in running it  but what exactly is the firm and how is  it all run  in their unprecedented interview with  oprah winfrey megan kept referring to  the firm  it was the queen's father king george vi  who first coined the phrase to  informally refer to the royal family  after harry and megan stepped away and  prince andrew stepped down from the  family the queen is said to have  appointed the firm of eight eight senior  working royals which includes herself  her daughter ann charles and camilla  william and kate and edward and sophie  they support the queen in her duties  like making public appearances  and diplomatic trips  but the active public lives of the  royals would not be possible without all  the departments and staff behind them  [Music]  senior working royal and their partner  have their own household made up of  staff and departments  there are literally thousands of people  working away behind the scenes to make  sure that everything runs smoothly and  the senior oils certainly depend on them  so they can carry out their official  duties the households are typically  named after buildings that they run from  so charles and camilla's is clarence  house and william and kate's is  kensington palace  there is a strict hierarchy and all  kinds of departments from hr to the  privy office and within it lots of  different roles from chefs to the lord  chamberlain the queen's household is the  largest and has an overarching advisory  role to the other households so how is  it all run  [Music]  it's made up of five main departments  first the private secretary's office sir  edward young has headed this up since  2017.  as the queen's private secretary he is  the main channel of communication  between her majesty and the government  he's in charge of her official program  and on a daily basis advises her on a  whole range of matters so he is  incredibly important and other senior  royals also have private secretaries who  carry out similar responsibilities it is  with great pleasure that i welcome you  all here tonight  the private secretary also organizes raw  speeches correspondence and official  presence for the public  the privy purse and treasurer's office  includes typical departments found in a  business like hr i.t and finance the  keeper of the privy purse and  treasurer's office is sir michael  stevens  next is the master of the households  department their remit is strictly  entertainment hospitality housekeeping  and catering so includes florists and  furniture upholsterers  vice admiral sir tony johnston byrd has  been master of the household since 2013.  the lord chamberlain's office is  responsible for organising events  including ceremonial activity like  honours state funerals raw weddings  garden parties and the opening of  parliament  lieutenant colonel michael vernon  fulfills this part-time role  finally there's the royal collection  trust which runs much like a museum  they're in charge of the public openings  of the royal family's residences  clarence house and kensington palace  have smaller but still sizable royal  households and with them many more  hundreds of staff that is a lot of  salaries so how were they paid for  earlier we mentioned the sovereign grant  which is managed by the keeper of the  privy purse and treasurer's office it's  an annual payment that's calculated  every year by the treasury and in  2021 that amount was 85.9 million so  that worked out as one pound and 29  pence per person in the uk now out of  that a core grant of 51.5  million pounds was paid towards funding  the firm's travel expenses and property  refurbishment also it goes towards  covering some of the salaries for staff  within the royal household except the  royal collection trust which is funded  by ticket sales  [Music]  and all this doesn't even include police  protection which is separately funded  and comes from an elite scotland yard  squad they provide 24-hour security for  the royals and rather than being  employed by the palace they're police  officers who apply to work for the royal  family  [Music]  it's not exactly clear how many people  and in what roles work for the royal  household there isn't a comprehensive  list publicly available with the  exception of the royal collection trust  which is published annually a quick look  at the palace's vacancies though and you  can see some of the jobs that are on  offer for example a gardener at windsor  castle or an executive assistant the  master of the household at buckingham  palace so it shows that running the firm  is far from a simple business  [Applause]  you

